At the author's explicit request, the HUD editor now ports Unity's root/group/
boolean/range row construction from HudEditorScreen.java, diagonal corner resize
calculation from HudResize.java, and CompactMotion.java (revision 5bbd639).
These Unity-owned implementations are adapted to Neon's armor/totem config,
native-resolution font renderer, Fabric input, and undo history. Unity's separate
checkout and installed artifacts are preserved; no Unity UI assets are bundled.
The HUD column also adapts HudEditorScreen.drawPanel/drawRange's translucent
layering, full-width rows, inline label/value presentation, whole-row slider
mapping and right-click numeric input, with Neon's quiet border and accent fills.

The inline color picker ports the interaction and HSV/alpha model from Unity's
ColorPicker.java, ClientScreen.java, and ColorArgumentType.java at revision
5bbd639, with Neon's layout, native typography, GPU gradients, and undo adapters.

Neon's six soft console-style UI cues and two chat pings are original deterministic synthesis, generated by
tools/generate-ui-sounds.ps1 and encoded as Ogg Vorbis. No Minecraft samples or
third-party audio assets are included.

Theme color linking and dark/readable surface roles adapt Unity's
ThemeColorRole.java, ThemePresets.apply(Color), and ClientScreen color-source
behavior, with Neon-specific persistence, alpha, Rainbow controls and Undo.

At the author's explicit request, HudFrameRate.java and HudFpsTransition.java
are copied from Unity revision 5bbd639 with only their package changed. The FPS
label/value rendering, reserved four-digit width, optional 120 ms number
smoothing and Background/Border/Shadow controls adapt HudManager.java,
HudPainter.java and HudEditorScreen.java to Minecraft's active font renderer,
theme colors, normalized HUD placement, profiles and Undo. Unity remains untouched.

At the author's explicit request, Better Chat adapts BetterChatModule.java and
the duplicate grouping, styled name highlighting, and entry animation from
MixinChatComponent.java in Unity revision 5bbd639. Neon retains vanilla chat
fonts, links, signatures and original history, adds server-chat mention support,
and supplies independent message/mention pings and native settings. Unity's
checkout and installed artifacts are not modified.

At the author's explicit request, Better Screenshot ports ExtraScreenshotModule.java,
MixinScreenshot.java and WindowsImageClipboard.java from Unity revision 5bbd639.
The asynchronous clipboard worker, desktop image fallback and native Windows
CF_DIB transfer are adapted to Neon's bindings, persistence, silent local notices
and lifecycle. Vanilla PNG saving remains intact even when clipboard copying fails.
